Capturing short-term price movements and trading activity with a single-factor approach
├─ Representing intraday shifts based on open–close price relationships
│   ├─ Using the relative position of open and close prices
│   │   ├─ open_to_prev_close_return: (open - prev_close) / prev_close
│   │   └─ close_to_prev_close_return: (close - prev_close) / prev_close
│   └─ Using the direction and magnitude of intraday price change
│       ├─ intraday_return: (close - open) / open
│       └─ intraday_sign: sign(close - open)  (1 = up, -1 = down)
├─ Characterizing intraday volatility structure based on high–low price range
│   ├─ Using the range between high and low prices
│   │   ├─ true_range: high - low
│   │   └─ normalized_range: (high - low) / prev_close
│   └─ Describing candlestick amplitude using high, low and close
│       ├─ upper_shadow: high - max(open, close)
│       ├─ body_size: abs(close - open)
│       └─ lower_shadow: min(open, close) - low
└─ Reflecting trading activity using volume and transaction amount
    ├─ Measuring activity intensity with volume
    │   └─ volume_ratio: volume / rolling_mean(volume, n)
    └─ Measuring capital participation using transaction amount
        └─ turnover_ratio: amount / rolling_mean(amount, n)